The exported `ChoiceDeck` must reject an empty option list, blank values or labels, and duplicate values with `Error`. It must copy its option objects so caller mutations cannot alter the deck. The initial value may be omitted; when supplied, it must identify an existing, non-disabled option or construction must throw.

`choose` must return `true` and change the selection only when the value identifies an enabled option different from the current selection. It returns `false` for unknown, disabled, or already-selected values. Failed selections must not change state or notify the listener. Successful selections invoke the optional listener exactly once after updating state. Listener exceptions propagate with the selection retained. `snapshot` must return fresh option objects in original order, the selected value, and direction `"rtl"` when requested or `"ltr"` otherwise.

